# Cortex style

Follow the Cortex engineering skill for every implementation and review:

`.cursor/skills/cortext-style/SKILL.md`

Always load:

- `references/review-philosophy.md`
- `references/architecture-and-api-review.md`
- `references/api-design-full-spec.md`
- `references/accepted-exceptions.md`
- `references/cortex-typescript-overlay.md`

Load subject rulebooks as needed (source-file basics, documentation, naming,
formatting, testing, implementation workflow).

## Non-negotiables (summary)

- Consumer-visible behavior first: success, failure, cancellation, retry.
- One owner / source of truth per lifecycle or state.
- Concrete types by default; interfaces only for real substitution or boundaries.
- Minimal public surface; do not leak transport, storage, or DI internals.
- Opt-in checks (e.g. `@cortex/networking` `.validate()`).
- Call `session.request` at the use site; map failures to layer semantic errors
  with `{ cause }`.
- Models under `models/` with JSDoc on every property; errors in `error/error.ts`.
- Smallest coherent change; delete superseded paths; update docs and tests with
  the code.
- Test public boundaries; do not export private helpers solely for tests.

Cite `CX-*` rule IDs in reviews. Do not invent stylistic rules beyond the
rulebooks and overlay.
